3,Kerewo language,https://grokipedia.com/page/kerewo_language,"Kerewo is a Papuan language of the Kiwaian branch within the Trans-New Guinea phylum, spoken by approximately 2,200 people primarily in villages downstream from Kikori station in the Kikori District of Gulf Province, Papua New Guinea.",Kerewo,Trans-New Guinea
